# A generic task over a list of lists (the stdlib's flatten, a `list of list of t`) handed a list of lists of numbers
# built by pushing lists. term test builds a tree-shaken program, and there the generic parameter's inner lists must be
# spelled as the caller's are: on Rust `fn flatten(lists: &[Vec<T>])` against `Vec<Rc<RefCell<Vec<i64>>>>` did not
# build, on Swift `flatten<T>(lists: [[T]])` against `[SeedList<Int>]` did not (term-self-host-001-1149, 1150).

load @term/base/list
  find list
  find flatten
  find join

task three
  like list
    like number
  save out
    make list
  call out/push
    code 1
  call out/push
    code 2
  call out/push
    code 3
  send back, read out

task two-threes
  like list
    like list
      like number
  save out
    make list
  call out/push
    call three
  call out/push
    call three
  send back, read out

test <flatten of a saved list of pushed lists>
  save nested
    call two-threes
  want hold
    call is-equal
      call join
        call flatten
          read nested
        text <,>
      text <1,2,3,1,2,3>

test <flatten of a list of pushed lists handed straight in>
  want hold
    call is-equal
      call join
        call flatten
          call two-threes
        text <,>
      text <1,2,3,1,2,3>
